{
  "name": "sam",
  "description": "SAM (Software Automatic Mouth) is a tiny C text-to-speech synthesizer, a C adaptation of the 1982 Commodore C64 speech program. It pairs a text-to-phoneme converter (reciter) with a phoneme-to-speech routine, plays audio live via SDL2 or writes .wav files, and this fork adds a unified Windows/Linux CMake/vcpkg build plus golden-fixture stage-dump instrumentation for a planned Python reimplementation.",
